I've committed the fix as 8aa7983e, and all of the owner's done-when for #1187 now holds. A unit test that reaches an exit door now fails under its own name, instead of killing the whole test binary with no test named, which is what kept main red for about 16 hours. cargo fmt --check, clippy with -D warnings, cargo build and cargo test (43 suites) all pass.

What changed:
• One exit door. dispatch_sub::exit_process(code) -> ! calls std::process::exit in the real binary. In the unit-test build it panics with a message naming #1187.
• Sites routed through it: 9 in dispatch_sub.rs, 1 in config_syntax.rs, plus 11 in cli.rs, 1 in config.rs (refuse_if_not_toml) and 1 in project_base_url.rs. The plan only listed the first two. I converted the others because unit tests call the functions they sit in (parse_args_with_config, load_config_file, resolve_base_url), so the done-when couldn't be met without them. Each was a one-token swap, and the real binary behaves exactly as before.
• Lint test un-ignored. test_try_dispatch_subcommand_lint now tests a new lint_shell_status function, which holds the lint arm's decision. It uses lint zz (expects 2) and lint fix (expects the "needs an interactive session" code), so the real linter never runs. It also checks that the door panics.
• Guard test. The new tests/process_exit_sites.rs requires every direct process::exit in src/ to be registered by file and count. Otherwise it fails, naming the file and line. A count that goes up or down fails too.

Checks I ran:
• I added a stray exit(3) with a NEUTERED marker. The guard failed with "registered 1, found 2 at line(s) [155, 220]". After restoring it (0 markers left), the guard passed.
• I added a temporary test that reaches the lint arm's exit. It was reported by name as zz_reaches_the_lint_exit ... FAILED, and the other 88 dispatch tests still passed. Removed afterwards.
• The two tests that check lint exit codes through the built binary still pass.

Remaining direct exits: six, and no unit test can reach any of them:
• exit_process itself, whose exit line isn't compiled into the test build.
• Four in main.rs, which only main() reaches.
• One in prompt/sigterm.rs, which runs only when a real signal arrives.

Issue #1187: the commit title keeps "Part of #1187" as the task asked, but the body says Fixes #1187, so the issue closes when this is pushed. I posted the census table and both checks on #1187, and added an entry to ARCHITECTURE.md.

test_try_dispatch_subcommand_test is still #[ignore], for its own reason: it runs cargo test inside cargo test. If someone runs it with --ignored and it fails, it now panics instead of killing the binary.
